# HOS-UI program page — applies when your ticket belongs to HOS-UI

## Standing law

You are working in `HumanifyOS`. The complete specification of what you build lives in the `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/` tree at the root of this
repository (the HOSPACK/HOS-UI build pack, mounted as a submodule or copy; `HOSPACK/` = HOS + HOS-UI + HOS-Admin, three programs side by side): `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/<MODULE>/spec/**` (freeze, architecture, schema + SQL,
OpenAPI, events, config keys, auth/tenancy, processes, fixtures, screens), `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/api/`, `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/schema/`, `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/JIRA_IMPORT.json`
(every ticket), `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/plan/BUILD_MAP.html` (what runs now). Nothing is designed in chat: if a contract, table, event, key, route or
screen is not in `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/` (or, for the platform, in `HOSPACK/HOS/`), it does not exist yet — say so instead of inventing it.

**HOS-UI is the HumanifyOS end-user application program (HOSAppServer `hos-appserver` :8140, `hos-ws` :8141, `hos-seed`, the TTEC Quality UI for the Agent, Supervisor, Ops Leader and VoC personas).** The platform contract it builds on lives in the sibling pack `HOSPACK/HOS/` at the same repository root (LOOM, SWATCH, RUBRIC, CORE: OpenAPI, SQL, events, auth/tenancy, config keys, the base preamble `HOSPACK/HOS/LOOM/spec/CURSOR_PREAMBLE.md`, `HOSPACK/HOS/api/`, `HOSPACK/HOS/schema/`) — it is **read-only for HOS-UI agents**: never edit `HOSPACK/HOS/**`, never add a route, table or event there, never take a HOS ticket. `HOSPACK/HOS-Admin/**` (the administration program: AdminServer :8150, the Admin UI, migrations 0030–0039) is a sibling pack too — read-only here; the Admin persona and the `/admin/*` routes left HOS-UI in v3.0. HOS-UI code lives only in apps/app/*, internal/app, pkg/contracts/app (Go) and apps/web/quality, packages/ui/src/quality, packages/contracts/app, services/mock-api app fixtures (TS); everything else in the repository belongs to HOS or the other sibling program. HOS-UI starts when HOS gate G-READY is green (`scripts/hos-ready.sh`; prerequisites in `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/plan/hos_prerequisites.json`) **and** HOS-Admin gate G-RBAC is green (its roles/RBAC + `POST /v1/admin/audit/events` are live — `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/INFRA-FROM-HOS-ADMIN.md`, `plan/hos_admin_prerequisites.json`); HOS-UI consumes HOS-Admin (audit writer client, effective roles, the rubric-builder deep link) and is never a dependency of HOS or HOS-Admin.

## Folders HOSPACK/HOS-UI owns in this repository

- `apps/app/hos-appserver`
- `apps/app/hos-ws`
- `apps/app/hos-seed`
- `internal/app`
- `pkg/contracts/app (generated)`
- `migrations/0017…0021, 0026`

Everything else — the workbench, LOOM/SWATCH/RUBRIC/CORE processes, `pkg/lib`, `pkg/common`, `packages/{api,features,ui,platform}` roots, deploy, CI — is HOS's
(and the other consumer program's folders are its own); a HOSPACK/HOS-UI ticket never changes it (a needed platform change is a HOS ticket, filed through the pack, never done in passing).

## How a HOSPACK/HOS-UI ticket is done

1. The ticket is `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/JIRA_IMPORT.json` → `projects[0].issues[externalId == <ID>]` (ids `A-*`, `Q-*`, `X-*`, `M-20…M-24`, `M-26`); touch only its lock units.
2. Preambles, in order: `HOSPACK/HOS/LOOM/spec/CURSOR_PREAMBLE.md` (base, read-only) → `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/APP/spec/CURSOR_PREAMBLE.md` → the program preamble `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/spec/CURSOR_PREAMBLE.md`.
3. Contracts: `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/APP/spec/openapi/openapi-app.yaml` is HOSPACK/HOS-UI's; LOOM/CORE/RUBRIC contracts are read from `HOSPACK/HOS/<MODULE>/spec/openapi/` and never edited.
   Routes live in `apps/app/hos-appserver/server`, domain code in `internal/app/<pkg>`; platform calls go only through `pkg/lib/invoke` (Dapr service invocation, Bearer forwarded).
4. Before the PR: `make codegen test lint spec-lint arch-lint`, `make app-openapi-check`, `make app-e2e`, `scripts/app-live-smoke.sh`. One named test per acceptance criterion; PR body = `RESULT.json`.
5. Prerequisites from HOS (what must be merged and running before a HOSPACK/HOS-UI ticket can be proven live) are in `HOSPACK/HOS-UI/plan/hos_prerequisites.json`;
   `scripts/hos-ready.sh` is green (HOS gate G-READY) and HOS-Admin's G-RBAC probes answer (`GET :8150/v1/_auth/probe`, `POST /v1/admin/audit/events`) is the readiness contract — never work around a red readiness check.

Skill `.claude/skills/hosui-app/SKILL.md` explains how to add things the HOSPACK/HOS-UI way and which commands to run.

